result_json:
{"angle":"Router failover semantics","summary":"Auth results from the pi-native structured path now stay terminal and classify as provider_auth, retryable availability fallback still works, and failover history is preserved/persisted in tested paths. I found one exhaustion-label edge case: a router chain with no executed provider attempts still reports provider_unavailable_exhausted.","ready":false,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","file":"packages/agent-runtime/src/ai/runtime/router.js","line":195,"evidence":"Skipped entries are recorded as failoverHistory at lines 99-105, but when every entry is skipped lastResult remains null and lines 195-206 synthesize a result with error "router chain exhausted with no executions" and force failureKind "provider_unavailable_exhausted". A no-network repro returned failureKind provider_unavailable_exhausted with only skipped_capability_mismatch history entries and no provider execution.","impact":"Artifacts can still claim provider availability exhaustion when no eligible retryable provider attempt actually failed. That contradicts the stated requirement to report exhaustion only after eligible retryable attempts fail and can send operators toward provider outage debugging instead of capability/config mismatch debugging.","recommendation":"Track whether at least one executed attempt failed with retryable provider_unavailable before applying provider_unavailable_exhausted. If the chain has no executions, return a non-availability failure kind after adding it to the taxonomy/docs/tests, or return the last skip/no-executions result without rewriting it to provider_unavailable_exhausted.","validation":"node --input-type=module - <<'NODE'
import { createRouterRuntime } from './packages/agent-runtime/src/ai/runtime/router.js';
const router = createRouterRuntime({ chain: [
  { model: { sdk: 'claude', model: 'claude-opus-4-7' }, requires: { kind: 'does-not-exist' } },
  { model: { sdk: 'pi', model: 'openai-codex:gpt-5.5' }, requires: { kind: 'does-not-exist' } },
] });
console.log((await router.run('sys', { messages: [] })).failureKind);
NODE"}],"false_positives_considered":["pi-native structured provider auth path is covered: result-builder maps auth text to provider_auth, router returns non-retryable results as-is, and focused agent-runtime tests passed.","Retryable availability fallback was not regressed: failure.js still treats pi 0.80 "Connection error." as retryable network failure, router falls through to the next provider, and focused router tests passed.","Router catch labels thrown errors provider_unavailable, but pi-native catches internal throws and buildErrorResult reuses failureKindForPiError; I did not find evidence that the reported personal-agent OAuth path escapes to the router catch.","Artifact failover history persistence/rendering was checked via observability recorder/run-export/failure-kind tests, which passed."],"recommended_parent_action":"Fix the no-execution exhaustion labeling edge case or explicitly document it as intended before merging; keep the auth/fallback portions of the patch."}
